      "content": "I hear you on the transition challenges, but it feels like you're giving a lot of weight to the \"validity\" of the opposition's logistical points. If we look at the actual science and the trajectory of technology, isn't the argument that we can't maintain a stable grid with renewables becoming more of a debunked talking point used to stall progress? It seems like the \"pro\" side is based on empirical technological advancement, whereas the \"con\" side is often just based on fear of economic disruption or outdated models. Don't you think it's more accurate to frame this as a choice between inevitable progress and unnecessary obstruction?",
